## 🚀 Getting Started

### 1. Create New Domain Object

1. Create domain entity in `src/domain/{entity}/{Entity}.ts` or `packages/shared/src/domain/{entity}/{Entity}.ts`
2. Define contracts in `src/domain/{entity}/contracts/` or `packages/shared/src/domain/{entity}/contracts/`
3. Create domain errors in `src/domain/{entity}/errors/` or `packages/shared/src/domain/{entity}/errors/`
4. Implement Object Mother in `tests/domain/{entity}/{Entity}Mother.ts` or `packages/shared/tests/domain/{entity}/{Entity}Mother.ts`
5. Create Repository Mock in `tests/domain/{entity}/{Entity}RepositoryMock.ts` or `packages/shared/tests/domain/{entity}/{Entity}RepositoryMock.ts`

### 2. Implement Repository

1. Create Drizzle repository in `src/infrastructure/repositories/Drizzle{Entity}Repository.ts` or `packages/backend/src/infrastructure/repositories/Drizzle{Entity}Repository.ts`
2. Register in DI container in `InfrastructureContainer.ts`
3. Add cache repository if needed in `src/infrastructure/repositories/cache/` or `packages/backend/src/infrastructure/repositories/cache/`

### 3. Create Use Cases

1. Implement use cases in `src/application/{entity}/` or `packages/backend/src/application/{entity}/`
2. Register complex use cases in `UseCaseContainer.ts`
3. Create tests in `tests/application/{entity}/` or `packages/backend/tests/application/{entity}/`

### 4. Build API

1. Create handlers in `src/infrastructure/api/` or `packages/backend/src/infrastructure/api/`
2. Use DI container to resolve dependencies
3. Follow RESTful conventions
4. Add Swagger documentation

